+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| cacti-spine installed                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Copy the sample configuration and edit it before starting spine:

  cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/spine.conf.dist %%PREFIX%%/etc/spine.conf
  $EDITOR %%PREFIX%%/etc/spine.conf

spine requires raw socket access (CAP_NET_RAW) for ICMP polling. The
Linux --enable-lcap/setcap path is not available on FreeBSD. Choose one
of the following approaches based on site policy:

  1. setuid-root (simplest):
       chmod u+s %%PREFIX%%/sbin/spine

  2. Run Cacti's poller as root, which passes the privilege through to
     spine without requiring a setuid binary.

  3. Use security/sudo to grant the cacti user controlled invocation:
       cacti ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: %%PREFIX%%/sbin/spine

For use with Cacti, configure the poller path in Cacti's settings to
point to %%PREFIX%%/sbin/spine.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
